{"seq": 168, "type": "assistant_message", "ts": "2026-11-22T17:13:10.785937+00:00", "payload": {"reasoning": "", "text": "The implementation is complete and verified.\n\n**Design** (`/work/main.go`): all three nodes share state through Maelstrom's linearizable `lin-kv` service, so they trivially agree on every journal.\n\n- **Storage**: each journal is split into 32-entry chunks (`journals:<journal>:chunks:<n>`); a bookmark lives in its own key (`journal-bookmarks:<journal>`).\n- **append**: finds the first non-full chunk, reads it, then atomically appends with a single `cas` (`from` = old chunk, `to` = old chunk + entry). The CAS both allocates the position and stores the entry, so a position can never be duplicated, skipped, or lost; CAS conflicts are retried by re-reading. Positions are 0-based and contiguous per journal.\n- **fetch**: reads the chunk containing the requested position and returns contiguous `[position, entry]` pairs from that position onward (or omits the journal if nothing is available at/after it), so a reply never skips a position it passes.\n- **bookmark / bookmarks**: bookmarks advance monotonically via CAS; `bookmarks` returns only journals that have a bookmark.\n- Protocol is implemented under the renamed types/fields (`append/appended`, `fetch/fetched`, `bookmark/bookmarked`, `bookmarks/bookmarks_are`); library logging is silenced to keep stdout/stderr clean and fast.\n\n**Verification**: `go build -o node .` succeeds (also offline, `GOPROXY=off`), `go vet` clean, and the exact grading command was run three times independently at `--rate 1000 --time-limit 20`: all exited 0 with `Everything looks good!` (`:valid? true`, 0 fail-counts, no error types).", "tool_calls": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 68401, "output_tokens": 372}}}
